00:28:52.940 --> 00:28:54.469
people turn to the illicit street

00:28:54.470 --> 00:28:56.299
drugs and the overdoses go up.

00:28:56.300 --> 00:28:58.339
So isn't there ultimately

00:28:58.340 --> 00:29:00.289
even a case for saying,

00:29:00.290 --> 00:29:02.299
you know, just allow the legal sale

00:29:02.300 --> 00:29:04.399
of all of it and we need to

00:29:04.400 --> 00:29:06.379
build up a safety net

00:29:06.380 --> 00:29:08.509
around it? We need to build build up

00:29:08.510 --> 00:29:09.829
appropriate treatment centers.

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:11.719
And to your point, you know,

00:29:11.720 --> 00:29:13.639
put recovery up

00:29:13.640 --> 00:29:15.289
there, as you know, one of the top

00:29:15.290 --> 00:29:17.179
priorities and kind of learn

00:29:17.180 --> 00:29:19.249
to grapple with the reality

00:29:19.250 --> 00:29:21.289
of these drugs in a kind of

00:29:21.290 --> 00:29:22.782
more sophisticated manner society

00:29:24.020 --> 00:29:24.470
wide.

00:29:24.470 --> 00:29:26.239
Again I look to the Europeans

00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:27.799
because they're ahead of us on this.

00:29:27.800 --> 00:29:28.969
They had the open drug schemes in

00:29:28.970 --> 00:29:30.229
the late 80s. They made the same

00:29:30.230 --> 00:29:32.359
mistake that we are making now.

00:29:32.360 --> 00:29:33.919
They changed their approach.

00:29:33.920 --> 00:29:35.509
They involved law enforcement in the

00:29:35.510 --> 00:29:37.579
early 90s, and they fixed it.

00:29:37.580 --> 00:29:39.799
There are supervised

00:29:39.800 --> 00:29:41.689
drug use

00:29:41.690 --> 00:29:43.219
sites in the Netherlands.

00:29:43.220 --> 00:29:45.229
There's about 20.

00:29:45.230 --> 00:29:46.489
I just got the research I haven't

00:29:46.490 --> 00:29:48.619
published yet, but my my character

00:29:48.620 --> 00:29:49.649
gave me that information.

00:29:49.650 --> 00:29:51.319
There's about 20 supervised drug use

00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:52.999
sites in the Netherlands.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:54.709
They get between 10 and 20 people

00:29:54.710 --> 00:29:56.599
per day, and it's a tiny

00:29:56.600 --> 00:29:57.949
number of people, if you think about

00:29:57.950 --> 00:29:59.809
it. There are some

00:29:59.810 --> 00:30:01.729
people that they do give

00:30:01.730 --> 00:30:03.559
heroin to in the in

00:30:03.560 --> 00:30:05.209
the Netherlands, it's about 100.

00:30:05.210 --> 00:30:07.249
It's less than 150.

00:30:07.250 --> 00:30:08.749
Those are people for whom methadone,

00:30:08.750 --> 00:30:11.269
which is the substitute for heroin,

00:30:11.270 --> 00:30:12.679
did not work.

00:30:12.680 --> 00:30:15.319
Suboxone or buprenorphine

00:30:15.320 --> 00:30:17.329
is a superior or somewhat

00:30:17.330 --> 00:30:19.879
superior. People think to methadone

00:30:19.880 --> 00:30:21.949
is widely available.

00:30:21.950 --> 00:30:23.299
So I am.

00:30:23.300 --> 00:30:25.099
I'm on board with the Dutch model.

00:30:25.100 --> 00:30:27.019
I'm fine if you need to have some

00:30:27.020 --> 00:30:28.879
folks to allow

00:30:28.880 --> 00:30:30.679
them to use those harder drugs.

00:30:30.680 --> 00:30:32.779
But but they do not sell

00:30:32.780 --> 00:30:35.419
heroin or fentanyl in

00:30:35.420 --> 00:30:37.069
coffee shops in the same way that

00:30:37.070 --> 00:30:38.479
they do marijuana.

00:30:38.480 --> 00:30:40.439
Yeah, I will say

00:30:40.440 --> 00:30:42.319
I continue to

00:30:42.320 --> 00:30:43.729
think that the evidence points

00:30:43.730 --> 00:30:45.739
towards when you criminalize

00:30:45.740 --> 00:30:47.119
these substances, they tend to get

00:30:47.120 --> 00:30:48.289
more dangerous.

00:30:48.290 --> 00:30:50.929
However, you did raise this

00:30:50.930 --> 00:30:52.819
Dutch model with some

00:30:52.820 --> 00:30:55.249
activists this idea of

00:30:55.250 --> 00:30:57.109
offering an alternative to

00:30:57.110 --> 00:30:59.149
jail treatment as an alternative

00:30:59.150 --> 00:31:00.079
to jail.

00:31:00.080 --> 00:31:01.789
And I was kind of surprised that so

00:31:01.790 --> 00:31:03.619
many activists

00:31:03.620 --> 00:31:05.539
just said no, that that

00:31:05.540 --> 00:31:07.459
is not where

00:31:07.460 --> 00:31:08.329
we're going with this.

00:31:08.330 --> 00:31:10.099
We're not even talking about someone

00:31:10.100 --> 00:31:12.079
who's been arrested just

00:31:12.080 --> 00:31:13.849
for possession and somebody who's

00:31:13.850 --> 00:31:15.739
been doing breaking the law

00:31:15.740 --> 00:31:16.800
in some other way.

00:31:17.840 --> 00:31:19.669
And instead of sending you to jail,

00:31:19.670 --> 00:31:22.279
we can see you have an addiction.

00:31:22.280 --> 00:31:23.509
So we're going to divert you to

00:31:23.510 --> 00:31:24.829
treatment.

00:31:24.830 --> 00:31:26.839
Were you surprised at the pushback

00:31:26.840 --> 00:31:28.219
to that idea?

00:31:28.220 --> 00:31:29.119
I was.

00:31:29.120 --> 00:31:30.979
I was. Annoyed.

00:31:30.980 --> 00:31:32.839
I find myself still annoyed

00:31:32.840 --> 00:31:34.669
by it because

00:31:34.670 --> 00:31:36.299
that was not my understanding.

00:31:36.300 --> 00:31:38.389
Now, maybe I back in the 90s.

00:31:38.390 --> 00:31:39.589
I mean, and now maybe I

00:31:39.590 --> 00:31:40.729
misremembered it.

00:31:40.730 --> 00:31:41.779
Or maybe I.

00:31:41.780 --> 00:31:43.729
But I feel a little hoodwinked that

00:31:43.730 --> 00:31:45.709
there was this idea that

00:31:45.710 --> 00:31:46.849
we were going to. We were going to

00:31:46.850 --> 00:31:48.499
have rehab as the alternative to

00:31:48.500 --> 00:31:49.459
prison.

00:31:49.460 --> 00:31:50.779
But then when it came time to

00:31:50.780 --> 00:31:52.819
implement these things,

00:31:52.820 --> 00:31:54.229
I think it was also just a thing on

00:31:54.230 --> 00:31:55.099
the left.

00:31:55.100 --> 00:31:56.569
I mean, maybe the right to, but I

00:31:56.570 --> 00:31:58.459
know the left better, which is that

00:31:58.460 --> 00:31:59.809
like, you kind of get a little bit

00:31:59.810 --> 00:32:00.949
and you keep pushing.

00:32:00.950 --> 00:32:02.029
I think they had just so much

00:32:02.030 --> 00:32:03.619
political power that progressives

00:32:03.620 --> 00:32:04.639
were just like, Well, we don't want

00:32:04.640 --> 00:32:05.899
to require anything like that.

00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:07.009
And I think that that plays into

00:32:07.010 --> 00:32:09.139
victim ideologies.

00:32:09.140 --> 00:32:11.089
So, yeah, I was bothered by

00:32:11.090 --> 00:32:12.409
it.

00:32:12.410 --> 00:32:13.879
I mean, just even at like a kind of

00:32:13.880 --> 00:32:16.579
political level, you'd kind of go,

00:32:16.580 --> 00:32:18.679
Well, wouldn't that be progress?

00:32:18.680 --> 00:32:19.669
Like, wouldn't that like if you're

00:32:19.670 --> 00:32:22.069
trying to legalize all drugs

00:32:22.070 --> 00:32:24.409
and you're like in a conservative

00:32:24.410 --> 00:32:25.789
part of the United States and you're

00:32:25.790 --> 00:32:27.049
like, Well, we're just saying let

00:32:27.050 --> 00:32:28.549
the addicts go to rehab rather than

00:32:28.550 --> 00:32:30.299
prison, why would you oppose that?

00:32:30.300 --> 00:32:32.449
But they do, because they view

00:32:32.450 --> 00:32:34.759
it as it's not just a compromise,

00:32:34.760 --> 00:32:36.289
they view it as fundamentally

00:32:36.290 --> 00:32:38.659
immoral to require

00:32:38.660 --> 00:32:40.309
something of people.

00:32:40.310 --> 00:32:42.169
A place where it gets

00:32:42.170 --> 00:32:43.909
even a little more puzzling, I would

00:32:43.910 --> 00:32:45.709
say, is where we you start to get

00:32:45.710 --> 00:32:48.139
into mental illness.

00:32:48.140 --> 00:32:50.089
And this idea

00:32:50.090 --> 00:32:52.609
of again offering

00:32:52.610 --> 00:32:54.949
some treatment

00:32:54.950 --> 00:32:57.019
path rather than

00:32:57.020 --> 00:32:59.029
